TASK 3: UNRESTRICTED FILE UPLOAD - FILTER BYPASS
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

1. Objective:
To attempt bypassing file-upload restrictions on a lab application using three distinct techniques without executing any uploaded payloads.

2. Bypass Techniques Summary Table:
+--------------------------------+--------------------------+--------------------------------------------------------+
| Technique Attempted            | Outcome (Blocked/Bypassed)| Root-Cause Explanation                                 |
+--------------------------------+--------------------------+--------------------------------------------------------+
| Direct Disallowed File Upload  | Blocked                  | Server checks client-side extension against blacklist. |
| Double-Extension Bypass        | Bypassed                 | Filter only checked final extension (e.g., .jpg.php).  |
| Case-Manipulation Bypass       | Bypassed                 | Filter was case-sensitive (e.g., file.PhP allowed).    |
| Content-Type Header Spoofing   | Bypassed                 | Server blindly trusted HTTP Content-Type header        |
|                                |                          | supplied in multipart form data (e.g., image/jpeg).    |
+--------------------------------+--------------------------+--------------------------------------------------------+

